# Command History
>You're going to type a lot of commands, and typing everything from scratch can be annoying. Luckily, the shell saves a history of every command you invoke.

## Solve:
-I just used the up arrow key to navigate the history.
```
bash
hacker@hello~command-history:~$ the flag is pwn.college{QY7PXaoCRSRE9J36zvYWq_dHboK.0lNzEzNxwiM4ETOwIzW}

## flag:
